The auxiliary space complexity is $O(n)$ (linear space).
Each recursive call `factorial(n-1)` adds a new stack frame to the call stack, storing local variables and return addresses. For `factorial(n)`, there will be $n$ nested calls before the base case is reached, leading to a call stack depth proportional to $n$.
```python
def factorial(n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    return n * factorial(n - 1)
```
